@startmindmap Window Fogging

title Window Fogging — Causes, Ventilation Modes, and What To Do

* Window Fogging\n(Beschlagene Scheiben)

** Why It Happens
*** Temperature difference\nbetween cold glass\nand warm moist cabin air
*** Moisture sources inside the car
**** Occupants breathing
**** Wet clothing / umbrellas
**** Rain entering the cabin

** Ventilation Modes
*** Umluft\n(Recirculation Mode)
**** Recycles air already inside the car\nNo fresh air from outside
**** Good for
***** Avoiding outside smells\n(tunnels, trucks)
***** Faster cabin cooling\n(recirculates already-cooled air)
**** Bad for
***** Demisting — recirculates\nmoist cabin air, making\nfogging worse
***** Long journeys —\nCO₂ builds up,\noccupants become drowsy
*** Frischluft\n(Fresh Air Mode)
**** Draws air in from outside
**** Good for
***** Demisting — brings in\ndrier outside air
***** Air quality on long journeys
**** Bad for
***** Avoiding outside odours

** AC (Air Conditioning)
*** Dehumidifies air by passing\nit over a cold evaporator coil\n— moisture condenses out
*** Umluft + AC
**** AC removes some moisture\neach pass, but occupants\ncontinuously add it back\nthrough breathing
**** Less effective for demisting
**** Better for fast cooling
*** Frischluft + AC
**** Best combination for demisting\n— drier outside air +\nAC removes remaining moisture
**** Better air quality

** What To Do When Windows Fog Up
*** Switch to **Frischluft** mode\n(NOT Umluft)
*** Turn ventilation **ON**\nand direct air at the windscreen
*** Switch **AC on**\nto actively remove moisture
*** Open windows **slightly**\nto let moist air escape
*** Use **rear window heater**\n(Heckscheibenheizung)
*** Do NOT turn ventilation off\nor keep all windows closed —\nthis traps moist air inside

@endmindmap
